=== Adhoc Refinement Constraints Sample ===
--- 1. Single dependent argument refinement ---
  FixedArray<int, 5>.GetSize() = 5
  FixedArray<int, 5>.Describe() = FixedArray<Size=5>
  FixedArray<string, 0>.GetSize() = 0
--- 2. Multiple dependent argument refinements ---
  Matrix<3, 4>.GetRows() = 3
  Matrix<3, 4>.GetCols() = 4
  Matrix<3, 4>.Describe() = Matrix<3x4>
--- 3. Mixed generic + dependent argument refinement ---
  Container<string, 8>.GetSize() = 8
  Container<string, 8>.Describe() = Container<Size=8>(value=hello)
--- 4. Method with single parameter refinement ---
  Process(42) accepted
--- 5. Method with multiple parameter refinements ---
  Range(min=10, max=90) accepted
--- 6. Constructor with parameter refinement ---
  Bounded(size=25)
  bounded.GetSize() = 25
--- 7. Indexer with parameter refinement ---
  SafeList[2] = 30
  SafeList[0] after set = 99
--- 8. Compound predicate with and ---
  Validate(512) within [0, 1024]
  Validate(0) within [0, 1024]
--- 9. Constructing type with valid dependent value ---
  FixedArray<int, 100>.GetSize() = 100
  Matrix<1, 1>.Describe() = Matrix<1x1>
--- 10. Calling method with valid literal argument ---
  Process(0) accepted
  Process(99) accepted
--- 11. Method with generic constraint and parameter refinement ---
  Show(Widget#7, count=3)
--- 12. Flow narrowing within method body ---
  UseNarrowed(42) -> narrowed=42
  UseNarrowed(0) -> narrowed=0
--- 13. Inheritance with fixed dependent value ---
  SmallArray : FixedArray<int, 10> constructed successfully
  (10 satisfies constraint Size >= 0)
--- 14. Forwarding dependent parameter with implication ---
  Wrapper<5> : FixedArray<string, 5> constructed successfully
  (Wrapper's N >= 0 implies FixedArray's Size >= 0)
--- 15. Abstract type refinement - same constraint (Liskov) ---
  StrictValidator.Validate(42) accepted (same constraint >= 0)
  StrictValidator.Validate(0) accepted (same constraint >= 0)
--- 16. Abstract type refinement - no constraint (Liskov) ---
  LenientValidator.Validate(99) accepted (no constraint)
  LenientValidator.Validate(0) accepted (no constraint)
--- 17. Abstract type refinement - weaker constraint (Liskov) ---
  WeakerProcessor.Process(50) accepted (weaker constraint >= 0)
  WeakerProcessor.Process(10) accepted (weaker constraint >= 0)
=== Adhoc Refinement Constraints Done ===
